virglrenderer: a lost app's dropped buffer keeps an empty stand-in; the log names the apps' share

What: virgl-gpu-guard-desktop-reserve.patch drops the storage of a buffer an app made past
its share (the app's context is lost, the buffer gives its memory back). But the app may
already have handed that buffer to the compositor (a Wayland buffer; a lost app whose guest
driver was not told goes on and hands over new ones). Hyprland then imports it (attach) and
draws it (a sampler view): the handle had no storage, the command named a resource that was
not there, and Hyprland's context was lost too: a black VM, the same as 3.0.3 with a refused
handle. Now a dropped buffer keeps an empty 1x1 stand-in with the same target, format and
layers (vrend_renderer_resource_stand_in), charged nothing: Hyprland's commands find a
resource, the window shows empty, nothing else changes. Transfers that name the old size
fail on the stand-in as they did on the missing storage (no context is lost by ctx 0).
Also: an app's own resource refused at the apps' share was logged as "budget of N MB
reached" (the whole budget). It now says "apps' share of N MB reached (the last M MB of the
B MB budget are kept for the desktop)", with the context; Venus memory the same.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-resource-budget.c modes dropped and wording (fail without this patch).
